data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":351,"item_id":"fc_0841f4c0202f7d6f016ae21794d15881918f1e5672e8df193c","output_index":4,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":3,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/6/statement\",\"value\":\"LR.N2 p l M x y v ∧ (∀ q : ℚ, q ∈ LR.localRing p ↔ ∃ a d : ℤ, ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ d ∧ q = (a : ℚ)/d)\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/6/explanation\",\"value\":\"Factorials below p are units in R, so choose(l,j) is a unit. Compose the partial identities, invert the scalar, and deduce all matrix units preserve MR. Package the scalar-extension basis and span statements, and re-export T004's exact fraction description so later arithmetic workers can use it without bypassing the N002 source boundary.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/16/statement\",\"value\":\"LR.N4 K p l M x y h v ∧ ∃ b : ℂ, LR.Generates p M y v b ∧ LR.ScaledBasis p l M y v b\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/16/explanation\",\"value\":\"For r≤l<p, r! remains nonzero. Transport r! X_r=x^r and the y identity from M, then reduce the matrix-unit factorization on each scalar-extended basis. For any basis with the same generator matrices the polynomial expression has the same matrix, so the same unit formula holds. Invariance under powers, scalars and compositions gives invariance under all units. Retain existence of a generating scalar and its R-basis from N003, so the universal construction of beta is explicitly nonvacuous.\"}]}}"}

