SO64_h689CBMQiO2OuPCddsnVubXk2WW9KoL425Tz6SUe63QDw9rm71eCMPYsoo7lDzqrRWR2GIHlCaGfiPY2Q2GabtGg1sw5scODPN82VBsAXHio9s3AX6ZCPB_vG1dmw_H_hqGY_OjzOVqnfvqVcYHCUMOkTo01_Et3Pk5tig4E7IGwSkDZQc5XbFkI5E4-jK1jcXavfdA2qvcC4OsmyYoWu_xPuWog6Ma4A3DSujVA02Z7dtKF0m3oWydvzcgN-v0d2IcHR8kk_6tAYsbQ9nsf30SG_IkC290KJj5iNByk5gwsh0yfHJqp4rev8NAYj3NGVqkC0CeovkgrngpsUvW2JZ8whWt6rcVafbm3rUBfzG6CQIwYerkJ3bWTFgOpEl5uOjFLNjtUePoTDfhm0Z6Ym68ZPEYpeCzCZoyGSwe-1ZhsjutqNLluK_Iv14-tz14UBuRYEZl7-R3EAEdL24TRC-oSL9hvLi-QZ16bfee8tK5LsKqmMumIrCirsCRK4ZuxbIOYLNg=="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0841f4c0202f7d6f016ae21794d15881918f1e5672e8df193c","call_id":"call_8d0dd2f20d9845ad94f918a308ea1907","name":"check_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_candidate\":3,\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/6/statement\",\"value\":\"LR.N2 p l M x y v ∧ (∀ q : ℚ, q ∈ LR.localRing p ↔ ∃ a d : ℤ, ¬ (p : ℤ) ∣ d ∧ q = (a : ℚ)/d)\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/6/explanation\",\"value\":\"Factorials below p are units in R, so choose(l,j) is a unit. Compose the partial identities, invert the scalar, and deduce all matrix units preserve MR. Package the scalar-extension basis and span statements, and re-export T004's exact fraction description so later arithmetic workers can use it without bypassing the N002 source boundary.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/16/statement\",\"value\":\"LR.N4 K p l M x y h v ∧ ∃ b : ℂ, LR.Generates p M y v b ∧ LR.ScaledBasis p l M y v b\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/steps/16/explanation\",\"value\":\"For r≤l<p, r! remains nonzero. Transport r! X_r=x^r and the y identity from M, then reduce the matrix-unit factorization on each scalar-extended basis. For any basis with the same generator matrices the polynomial expression has the same matrix, so the same unit formula holds. Invariance under powers, scalars and compositions gives invariance under all units. Retain existence of a generating scalar and its R-basis from N003, so the universal construction of beta is explicitly nonvacuous.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report an actual obstacle using these five direct fields. Countercheck the alleged implication against the complete definitions, quantifiers and inequality directions; a feasible example alone does not determine an extremum. A fact not yet proved or registered in the current draft is an obligation to complete, not by itself a gap. For a mathematical stop, identify the concrete implication and actual mathematical difficulty encountered during normal checking/completion, not merely unfilled inventory or exposition. No fixed time/attempt count or counterexample is required. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP/SUSPECTED_GAP stop for an actual supported mathematical obstruction; INPUT_CONFLICT stops for incompatible inputs. In NL0, use source retrieval and explicit conditional deferral for unavailable primary texts; MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT requires that no complete secondary statement can be obtained. Other stages may report SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE for an actual access obstacle. Ordinary unfinished work is not an obstacle report. No mathematical acceptance is generated.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_arti